<header><h1>Infantry Tokens: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_infantry_tokens">Infantry Tokens</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>As each player only has twelve plastic infantry figures, a player cannot have infantry on more than twelve planets or being transported in more than twelve space areas, or any combination thereof.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Are fighter and infantry tokens limited, and what are they for?&rdquo;: &ldquo;each stack of tokens must sit with at least one plastic piece of the same type. So your plastic fighters and infantry limit how many places you can have them.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Infantry tokens are not component limited.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Is there a limit to how many infantry can be on one planet?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; any number of infantry can be on a planet. You are only limited by your components, and tokens can stand in for extra infantry.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 23.4: &ldquo;Units are limited to those included in the game, except for fighters and ground forces.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may remove a plastic infantry figure from a planet or space area, along with any accompanying infantry tokens, if doing so allows them to swap it into the active system and allows them to commit ground forces to and fight ground combats on multiple planets during the <b>Invasion</b> step of the tactical action in that system when they could otherwise not do so.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Yin4Life, Apr 22, 2019), on placing ground forces on a 13th planet: &ldquo;You place the units one at a time, so when you place on the 13th planet, you&rsquo;d have to remove a plastic ground force from somewhere that you already placed one.&rdquo; Covers placing, not committing.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Are fighter and infantry tokens limited, and what are they for?&rdquo;: &ldquo;You may swap a plastic piece on the board for a token at any time to free the plastic for use elsewhere.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player has an infantry token that is not accompanied by a plastic infantry and cannot replace it, the token is removed instead of destroyed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When you exceed the number of plastic infantry/fighters available, are unaccompanied tokens removed or destroyed? A: Removed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
